  "prompt": "Are doctors' professional fees subject to VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "09751a6e038bde9324af9a05213d9c92295e3eb9",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre doctors' professional fees subject to Value-Added Tax (VAT)?\n\n### Short Answer\nDoctors' professional fees are generally subject to VAT unless specifically exempted under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, doctors should assess whether their services qualify for any VAT exemptions. For instance, if a doctor provides services that are considered essential medical care, they may be exempt from VAT. However, if the services are deemed non-essential or fall outside the scope of exemptions, the doctor must charge VAT on their professional fees. It is advisable for medical practitioners to consult with a tax professional to ensure compliance with VAT regulations and to determine the applicability of any exemptions to their specific services.",
